Makefile: honor CXXFLAGS and LDFLAGS

The aws_kms_pkcs11.so link rule ignores the standard CXXFLAGS and
LDFLAGS variables, so flags supplied by the build system never reach
the compiler or linker.

For native builds this drops "-Wl,-rpath,${STAGING_LIBDIR_NATIVE}", so
the module is linked without a RUNPATH. When it is dlopen()ed, its
dependencies (the AWS SDK libraries, libcrypto.so.3, libjson-c.so.5) are
then resolved from the build machine instead of the native sysroot, and
loading fails unless LD_LIBRARY_PATH is set.

Pass the standard flags to the module build so the build system can set
compiler flags and the library search path. CPPFLAGS is not passed
separately because the build system already folds it into CXXFLAGS.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Chris Trowbridge <chris.trowbridge@ezurio.com>

--- a/Makefile
+++ b/Makefile
@@ -187,8 +187,8 @@
         aws_kms_pkcs11_test.c -o aws_kms_pkcs11_test -ldl
 
 aws_kms_pkcs11.so: aws_kms_pkcs11.cpp unsupported.cpp aws_kms_slot.cpp debug.cpp util.cpp attributes.cpp certificates.cpp
-	$(CXX) -shared -fPIC -Wall -I$(AWS_SDK_PATH)/include $(PKCS11_INC) $(JSON_C_INC) $(PROXY_CFLAGS) -fno-exceptions -std=c++17 $(SRC) \
-	    -o aws_kms_pkcs11.so $(STATIC_LIBS) $(LIBS) -lcrypto -ljson-c -lcurl -lz
+	$(CXX) -shared -fPIC -Wall -I$(AWS_SDK_PATH)/include $(PKCS11_INC) $(JSON_C_INC) $(PROXY_CFLAGS) -fno-exceptions -std=c++17 $(CXXFLAGS) $(SRC) \
+	    -o aws_kms_pkcs11.so $(LDFLAGS) $(STATIC_LIBS) $(LIBS) -lcrypto -ljson-c -lcurl -lz
 
 install: aws_kms_pkcs11.so
 	mkdir -p $(DESTDIR)$(PKCS11_MOD_PATH)
